# GMAIL.md — Gmail Access Reference

{{USER_NAME}}'s Gmail (`{{USER_PRIMARY_EMAIL}}`) is already authenticated. All Gmail work goes through one path: the `gog-firewall` CLI.

---

## The Rule: gog-firewall for Everything

| Goal | Use | Why |
|------|-----|-----|
| **Read / search** | **`gog-firewall gmail` CLI** | Goes through the prompt-injection firewall, the desired security path for inbound content. |
| **Write** (mark read, label, send, delete, draft) | **`gog-firewall gmail` CLI** | Full read+write OAuth scopes on a long-lived token. |

**The Gmail MCP connector (`mcp__claude_ai_Gmail__*`) is retired for Gmail work.** Its auth lapses constantly (frequent re-auth, tools silently absent in headless runs) and it lacks write scopes, so nothing load-bearing may depend on it. Expect occasional firewall false-positive redactions on very long emails (marketing, newsletters, recruiter walls); handle per Gotcha 9.

**Never use raw `gog gmail` for reads** — bypasses the firewall. Use `gog-firewall`.

**Tool path:** `{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/gog-firewall`

---

## CLI Command Surface (curated)

### Read
| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `gmail search <query>` | Search threads using Gmail query syntax. Returns **`.threads[]`** (not messages). |
| `gmail messages search <query>` | Search at the message level (rare; usually you want threads). |
| `gmail get <messageId>` | Get a **single message**. Modes: `full` (default) / `metadata` / `raw`. |
| `gmail thread get <threadId>` | Get a **full thread** (all messages in it). |
| `gmail thread attachments <threadId>` | List attachments across the thread. |
| `gmail attachment <msgId> <attId>` | Download a single attachment. |
| `gmail url <threadId>...` | Print the Gmail web URL for a thread (handy for handing off to {{USER_NAME}}). |
| `gmail history` | Gmail history API (delta sync; rarely needed). |

### Organize (writes)
| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `gmail thread modify <threadId> --add X --remove Y --no-input` | Add/remove labels on **all messages in the thread**. |
| `gmail labels list` | List all labels. |
| `gmail labels get <nameOrId>` | Label details + counts. |
| `gmail labels create <name>` | Create a label. |
| `gmail labels modify <threadId>... --add/--remove ...` | Same as `thread modify` but for many threads in one call. |
| `gmail batch modify <messageId>... --add/--remove ...` | Batch label ops at the **message** level. |
| `gmail batch delete <messageId>...` | Permanent delete — destructive, confirm first. |

### Write
| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `gmail send` | Send an email. Required: `--to`, `--subject`, `--body` (or `--body-file -` for stdin). |
| `gmail drafts list / get / create / update / delete / send` | Full draft lifecycle. |
| `gmail settings ...` | Gmail settings + admin. |

**`gog auth ...`** subcommands are exempt from the firewall — run them directly (`gog auth status`, `gog auth list`) for OAuth troubleshooting.

